(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test04_2B"] = [{"id":"79dec1e1","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Art scholars have noted that some colors seem to be more ______ viewers than others. For example, people tend to find paintings featuring blues and greens more appealing than paintings featuring yellows and oranges.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Art scholars have noted that some colors seem to be more ______ viewers than others. For example, people tend to find paintings featuring blues","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and greens more appealing than paintings featuring yellows and oranges.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["confusing for","attractive to","corrected by","similar to"]},{"id":"82cb7dda","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The field of study called affective neuroscience seeks instinctive, physiological causes for feelings such as pleasure or displeasure. Because these sensations are linked to a chemical component (for example, the release of the neurotransmitter dopamine in the brain when one receives or expects a reward), they can be said to have a partly physiological basis. These processes have been described in mammals, but Jingnan Huang and his colleagues have recently observed that some behaviors of honeybees (such as foraging) are also motivated by a dopamine-based signaling process. What choice best describes","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The field of study called affective neuroscience seeks instinctive, physiological causes for feelings such as pleasure or displeasure. Because","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"these sensations are linked to a chemical component (for example, the release of the neurotransmitter dopamine in the brain when one receives","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"or expects a reward), they can be said to have a partly physiological basis. These processes have been described in mammals, but Jingnan","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Huang and his colleagues have recently observed that some behaviors of honeybees (such as foraging) are also motivated by a dopamine-based","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"signaling process.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It describes an experimental method of measuring the strength of physiological responses in humans.","It illustrates processes by which certain insects can express how they are feeling.","It summarizes a finding suggesting that some mechanisms in the brains of certain insects resemble mechanisms in mammalian brains.","It presents research showing that certain insects and mammals behave similarly when there is a possibility of a reward for their actions."]},{"id":"a87c3925","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Soy sauce, made from fermented soybeans, is noted for its umami flavor. Umami —one of the five basic tastes along with sweet, bitter, salty, and sour — was formally classified when its taste receptors were discovered in the 2000s. In 2007, to define the pure umami flavor scientists Rie Ishii and Michael O Mahony used broths made from shiitake mushrooms and kombu seaweed, and two panels of Japanese and US judges closely agreed on a description of the taste. Text 2 A 2022 experiment by Manon J ünger et al. led to a greater understanding of soy sauce’s flavor profile. The team initially presented a mixture of compounds with low molecular weights to taste testers who found it was not as salty or bitter as real soy sauce. Further analysis of soy sauce identified proteins, including dipeptides, that enhanced umami flavor and also contributed to saltiness. The team then made a mix of 50 chemical compounds that’re-created soy sauce’s flavor.’","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Soy sauce, made from fermented soybeans, is noted for its umami flavor. Umami—one of the five basic tastes along with sweet, bitter, salty, and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sour—was formally classified when its taste receptors were discovered in the 2000s. In 2007, to define the pure umami flavor scientists Rie Ishii","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"and Michael O’Mahony used broths made from shiitake mushrooms and kombu seaweed, and two panels of Japanese and US judges closely","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"agreed on a description of the taste.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"A 2022 experiment by Manon Jünger et al. led to a greater understanding of soy sauce’s flavor profile. The team initially presented a mixture of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"compounds with low molecular weights to taste testers who found it was not as salty or bitter as real soy sauce. Further analysis of soy sauce","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"identified proteins, including dipeptides, that enhanced umami flavor and also contributed to saltiness. The team then made a mix of 50","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"chemical compounds that’re-created soy sauce’s flavor.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, if Ishii and O Mahony (Text 1) and J ünger et al. (Text 2) were aware of the findings of both experiments, they would most likely agree with which statement?","choices":["On average, the diets of people in the United States tend to have fewer foods that contain certain dipeptides than the diets of people in Japan have.","Chemical compounds that activate both the umami and salty taste receptors tend to have a higher molecular weight than those that only activate umami taste receptors.","Fermentation introduces proteins responsible for the increase of umami flavor in soy sauce, and those proteins also increase the perception of saltiness.","The broths in the 2007 experiment most likely did not have a substantial amount of the dipeptides that played a key part in the 2022 experiment."]},{"id":"81da17d3","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Italian painters in the 1500s rarely depicted themselves in their work. Even more rare were self-portrait paintings that portrayed the artist as a painter. At the time, painting was not yet respected as a profession, so painters mostly chose to emphasize other qualities in their self-portraits, like their intellect or social status. In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci. A painting of his from around 1585 shows Carracci in front of an easel holding a palette. Text 2 In their self-portraits, Bolognese artists typically avoided referring to the act of painting until the mid-1600s. However, Lavinia Fontana’s 1577 painting, Self-Portrait at the Keyboard, stands out as the earliest example of such a work by an artist from Bologna. Although the artist is depicted playing music, in the background, one can spot a painting easel by a window.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Italian painters in the 1500s rarely depicted themselves in their work. Even more rare were self-portrait paintings that portrayed the artist as a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"painter. At the time, painting was not yet respected as a profession, so painters mostly chose to emphasize other qualities in their self-portraits,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"like their intellect or social status. In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci. A","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"painting of his from around 1585 shows Carracci in front of an easel holding a palette.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"In their self-portraits, Bolognese artists typically avoided referring to the act of painting until the mid-1600s. However, Lavinia Fontana’s 1577","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"painting, Self-Portrait at the Keyboard, stands out as the earliest example of such a work by an artist from Bologna. Although the artist is depicted","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"playing music, in the background, one can spot a painting easel by a window.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the underlined claim in Text 1?","choices":["Carracci and Fontana were among the most well-respected painters in Bologna at the time.","The depiction of Fontana in Self-Portrait at the Keyboard was intended to underscore the artist’s creativity.","Fontana likely inspired the reference to an easel and palette in Carracci’s painting.","Self-Portrait at the Keyboard was painted earlier than Carracci’s painting and also refers to the artist’s craft."],"underline":"In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci.","underline_segments":["In the city of Bologna, the first artist to depict themself painting was a man named Annibale Carracci."]},{"id":"a1d2c4d0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Pteropods are small swimming snails with thin, delicate calcium carbonate shells. These animals are thought to be especially vulnerable to ocean acidification due to calcium carbonate’s susceptibility to dissolution at lower pH values. Victoria L. Peck and colleagues recently found that the periostracum (a protective coating on pteropods’ outer shells) prevents this dissolution when intact. Moreover, the team was surprised to discover that even when the periostracum is breached, pteropods can still mitigate damage by rebuilding the inner shell wall.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Pteropods are small swimming snails with thin, delicate calcium carbonate shells. These animals are thought to be especially vulnerable to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ocean acidification due to calcium carbonate’s susceptibility to dissolution at lower pH values. Victoria L. Peck and colleagues recently found","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that the periostracum (a protective coating on pteropods’ outer shells) prevents this dissolution when intact. Moreover, the team was surprised","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to discover that even when the periostracum is breached, pteropods can still mitigate damage by rebuilding the inner shell wall.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To call for additional research on biological mechanisms that improve pteropod survival rates","To discuss a conclusion drawn in a study of calcium carbonate’s role in protecting the periostracum of pteropods","To address some of the ways ocean acidification has altered pteropod behavior over time","To present findings that suggest that a concern about the effects of ocean acidification on pteropod shells may be unwarranted"]},{"id":"a756aa95","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The province of Xoconochco was situated on the Pacific coast, hundreds of kilometers southeast of Tenochtitlan, the capital of the Aztec Empire. Because Xoconochco’s location within the empire was so ______, cacao and other trade goods produced there could reach the capital only after a long overland journey.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The province of Xoconochco was situated on the Pacific coast, hundreds of kilometers southeast of Tenochtitlan, the capital of the Aztec","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Empire. Because Xoconochco’s location within the empire was so ______, cacao and other trade goods produced there could reach the capital","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"only after a long overland journey.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["unobtrusive","concealed","approximate","peripheral"]},{"id":"f0be91b2","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Drivers who strongly believe that the toll they must pay to use the Lewis and Clark Bridge, which spans the Ohio River to connect Indiana and Kentucky, is currently too high are unlikely to be ______ a proposal to increase the toll. Advocates for a higher toll are likely to have more success if they instead direct their arguments toward a more persuadable segment of the population.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Drivers who strongly believe that the toll they must pay to use the Lewis and Clark Bridge, which spans the Ohio River to connect Indiana and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Kentucky, is currently too high are unlikely to be ______ a proposal to increase the toll. Advocates for a higher toll are likely to have more success","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"if they instead direct their arguments toward a more persuadable segment of the population.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["receptive to","apprised of","incensed by","cited in"]},{"id":"8d802289","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Cross-Text Connections","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Cross-Text Connections","passage":"Text 1 Dance choreographer Alvin Ailey’s deep admiration for jazz music can most clearly be felt in the rhythms and beats his works were set to. Ailey collaborated with some of the greatest jazz legends, like Charles Mingus, Charlie Parker, and perhaps his favorite, Duke Ellington. With his choice of music, Ailey helped bring jazz to life for his audiences. Text 2 Jazz is present throughout Ailey’s work, but it’s most visible in Ailey’s approach to choreography. Ailey often incorporated improvisation, a signature characteristic of jazz music, in his work. When managing his dance company, Ailey rarely forced his dancers to an exact set of specific moves. Instead, he encouraged his dancers to let their own skills and experiences shape their performances, as jazz musicians do.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Text 1","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Dance choreographer Alvin Ailey’s deep admiration for jazz music can most clearly be felt in the rhythms and beats his works were set to. Ailey","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"collaborated with some of the greatest jazz legends, like Charles Mingus, Charlie Parker, and perhaps his favorite, Duke Ellington. With his choice","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of music, Ailey helped bring jazz to life for his audiences.","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Text 2","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Jazz is present throughout Ailey’s work, but it’s most visible in Ailey’s approach to choreography. Ailey often incorporated improvisation, a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"signature characteristic of jazz music, in his work. When managing his dance company, Ailey rarely forced his dancers to an exact set of specific","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"moves. Instead, he encouraged his dancers to let their own skills and experiences shape their performances, as jazz musicians do.","indent":0}],"question":"Based on the texts, both authors would most likely agree with which statement?","choices":["Dancers who worked with Ailey greatly appreciated his supportive approach as a choreographer.","Ailey’s work was strongly influenced by jazz.","Audiences were mostly unfamiliar with the jazz music in Ailey’s works.","Ailey blended multiple genres of music together when choreographing dance pieces."]},{"id":"8fb67890","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Archaeologists have discovered a runestone in Norway that may contain the earliest example of written words in Scandinavia. Carbon dating at the discovery site revealed that the stone was likely carved between 1 and 250 CE. Runologist Kristel Zilmer believes the stone will be helpful in learning more about the use of runic alphabets in early Iron Age Scandinavia.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Archaeologists have discovered a runestone in Norway that may contain the earliest example of written words in Scandinavia. Carbon dating at","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the discovery site revealed that the stone was likely carved between 1 and 250 CE. Runologist Kristel Zilmer believes the stone will be helpful in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"learning more about the use of runic alphabets in early Iron Age Scandinavia.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main topic of the text?","choices":["Battles of the Iron Age","A runestone found in Norway","A new method for dating rock samples","The research interests of Kristel Zilmer"]},{"id":"25fc2534","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Marine archaeologists have found much of the wooden hull of a sixteenth-century ship in a flooded quarry in southeast England. When it is exposed to air and water, wood rots quickly unless it is protected by sediment that shields it from oxygen. Therefore, the discovered ship was likely ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Marine archaeologists have found much of the wooden hull of a sixteenth-century ship in a flooded quarry in southeast England. When it is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"exposed to air and water, wood rots quickly unless it is protected by sediment that shields it from oxygen. Therefore, the discovered ship was","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"likely ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["covered by a protective sediment layer in the quarry.","one of several other ships buried in the same quarry.","a confirmation of previous theories about the type of wood that was used in sixteenth-century ships.","first constructed much earlier than previously thought."]},{"id":"34c2e387","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Central Ideas and Details","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Central Ideas and Details","passage":"Jürgen Kocka and other historians of capitalism rarely discuss domestic capitalism in Africa before the period of European colonization, implicitly presenting capitalism as external to and imposed on Africa. Crislayne Alfagali and other Africanist scholars have shown, however, that in parts of Africa, returns-focused investment, the establishment of open markets for wage labor, and other features of capitalism predated colonization. One reason for this discrepancy is that historians of capitalism tend to focus on longitudinal economic data drawn from archival records, which do not exist for much of precolonial Africa.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jürgen Kocka and other historians of capitalism rarely discuss domestic capitalism in Africa before the period of European colonization,","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"implicitly presenting capitalism as external to and imposed on Africa. Crislayne Alfagali and other Africanist scholars have shown, however, that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"in parts of Africa, returns-focused investment, the establishment of open markets for wage labor, and other features of capitalism predated","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"colonization. One reason for this discrepancy is that historians of capitalism tend to focus on longitudinal economic data drawn from archival","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"records, which do not exist for much of precolonial Africa.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement about Alfagali and other Africanist scholars is best supported by information in the text?","choices":["They likely make use of different types of evidence than historians of capitalism typically rely on.","They likely differ from historians of capitalism in the methods they use to derive longitudinal economic data from archival records.","They likely have a different view about which activities should be considered capitalist in nature than historians of capitalism do.","They likely view capitalism as having been more beneficial for Africa than historians of capitalism do."]},{"id":"7f293254","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Art collectives, like the United States- and Vietnam-based collective The Propeller Group or Cuba’s Los Carpinteros, are groups of artists who agree to work together: perhaps for stylistic reasons, or to advance certain shared political ideals, or to help mitigate the costs of supplies and studio space. Regardless of the reasons, art collectives usually involve some collaboration among the artists.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Art collectives, like the United States- and Vietnam-based collective The Propeller Group or Cuba’s Los Carpinteros, are groups of artists who","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"agree to work together: perhaps for stylistic reasons, or to advance certain shared political ideals, or to help mitigate the costs of supplies and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"studio space. Regardless of the reasons, art collectives usually involve some collaboration among the artists. Based on a recent series of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"interviews with various art collectives, an arts journalist claims that this can be difficult for artists who are often used to having sole control over","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"their work.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from the interviews best illustrates the journalist’s claim?","choices":["“The first collective I joined included many amazingly talented artists, and we enjoyed each other’s company, but because we had a hard time sharing credit and responsibility for our work, the collective didn’t last.”","“We work together, but that doesn’t mean that individual projects are equally the work of all of us. Many of our projects are primarily the responsibility of whoever originally proposed the work to the group.”","“Having worked as a member of a collective for several years, it’s sometimes hard to recall what it was like to work alone without the collective’s support. But that support encourages my individual expression rather than limits it.”","“Sometimes an artist from outside the collective will choose to collaborate with us on a project, but all of those projects fit within the larger themes of the work the collective does on its own.”"]},{"id":"f8244f7c","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"North American Thrasher Mean Bill Size and Habitat Temperature Range Mean bill surface area Mean maximum temperature of warmest Mean minimum temperature of coldest Species 2 (cm ) month (°C) month (°C) Brown thrasher 1.86 30.40 −4.29 Bendire’s thrasher 1.98 36.57 0.24 Long-billed 2.24 35.27 8.82 thrasher Cozumel thrasher 2.28 33.27 18.21 Ocellated thrasher 3.26 27.56 5.45 It has been hypothesized that since birds can dissipate excess heat through their bills, bill size should increase with habitat temperature. To evaluate this hypothesis for a 2021 study, Charlotte Probst and colleagues gathered data on mean bill surface area of species of North American thrashers (genus: Toxostoma) as well as on climate conditions of the birds native habitats. Based on their data, Probst and colleagues concluded that the hypothesis was not fully supported.","passage_lines":[{"type":"table","title":"North American Thrasher Mean Bill Size and Habitat Temperature Range","headers":["Species","Mean bill surface area (cm²)","Mean maximum temperature of warmest month (°C)","Mean minimum temperature of coldest month (°C)"],"rows":[["Brown thrasher","1.86","30.40","−4.29"],["Bendire’s thrasher","1.98","36.57","0.24"],["Long-billed thrasher","2.24","35.27","8.82"],["Cozumel thrasher","2.28","33.27","18.21"],["Ocellated thrasher","3.26","27.56","5.45"]]},{"type":"text","text":"It has been hypothesized that since birds can dissipate excess heat through their bills, bill size should increase with habitat temperature. To evaluate this hypothesis for a 2021 study, Charlotte Probst and colleagues gathered data on mean bill surface area of species of North American thrashers (genus: Toxostoma) as well as on climate conditions of the birds native habitats. Based on their data, Probst and colleagues concluded that the hypothesis was not fully supported."}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support Probst and colleagues’ conclusion?","choices":["Although the Bendire’s thrasher has one of the smallest mean bill surface areas of the birds included in the table, its habitat has one of the lowest mean maximum temperatures in the warmest month and one of the lowest mean minimum temperatures in the coldest month.","Although the Cozumel thrasher has the second greatest mean bill surface area of the birds included in the table, its habitat’s mean temperature in the warmest month is significantly higher than that of the other birds’ habitats.","Of the birds included in the table, the brown thrasher has the smallest mean bill surface area and the habitat with the lowest mean minimum temperature in the coldest month, while the long-billed thrasher has the second-largest mean bill surface area and the habitat with the second- highest mean minimum temperature in the coldest month.","Of the birds included in the table, the ocellated thrasher has the largest mean bill surface area and the habitat with the lowest mean maximum temperature in the warmest month, while the Bendire’s thrasher has the second smallest mean bill surface area and the habitat with the highest mean maximum temperature in the warmest month."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["North American","Thrasher Mean Bill Size and Habitat Temperature","Range"]},{"id":"f495b554","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Silicon-based photovoltaic cells account for 95% of the cells used in solar panels worldwide despite converting an average of only 18 –22% of the sunlight that reaches them. In a study addressing this relative inefficiency, a team led by Laura Miranda-Pérez demonstrated that the addition of a thin layer of the mineral perovskite — which captures the blue range of light in the solar spectrum, whereas silicon captures the red range — allows the cells to convert 29.5% or more of the Sun’s energy into usable electricity. Cells made with only perovskite, however, are no more efficient than silicon-based ones. It’s reasonable to conclude, then, that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Silicon-based photovoltaic cells account for 95% of the cells used in solar panels worldwide despite converting an average of only 18–22% of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sunlight that reaches them. In a study addressing this relative inefficiency, a team led by Laura Miranda-Pérez demonstrated that the addition of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"a thin layer of the mineral perovskite—which captures the blue range of light in the solar spectrum, whereas silicon captures the red range—","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"allows the cells to convert 29.5% or more of the Sun’s energy into usable electricity. Cells made with only perovskite, however, are no more","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"efficient than silicon-based ones. It’s reasonable to conclude, then, that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["photovoltaic cells with both silicon and perovskite are more efficient because they make use of more of the solar spectrum.","photovoltaic cells with only perovskite and no silicon would likely convert more than 29.5% of the Sun’s energy.","solar power will remain elusive until photovoltaic cells are replaced with a more practical technology.","researchers need to evaluate whether other minerals like perovskite are as effective as perovskite seems to be."]},{"id":"0d7f4966","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Jean-Bernard Caron and colleagues recently discovered a cache of jellyfish fossils in the Burgess Shale, a site in the Canadian Rockies that is rich in fossils from the Cambrian period (over 500 million years ago). Caron and colleagues claim that these are the oldest jellyfish fossils ever discovered. In the past twenty years, two sites in China and the United States have yielded fossils of a similar age that some experts believe are most likely jellyfish due to their shapes and the appearance of projecting tentacles. But Caron and colleagues argue that the apparent tentacles are in fact the comb rows of ctenophores, gelatinous animals that are only distantly related to jellyfish.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jean-Bernard Caron and colleagues recently discovered a cache of jellyfish fossils in the Burgess Shale, a site in the Canadian Rockies that is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"rich in fossils from the Cambrian period (over 500 million years ago). Caron and colleagues claim that these are the oldest jellyfish fossils ever","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"discovered. In the past twenty years, two sites in China and the United States have yielded fossils of a similar age that some experts believe are","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"most likely jellyfish due to their shapes and the appearance of projecting tentacles. But Caron and colleagues argue that the apparent tentacles","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"are in fact the comb rows of ctenophores, gelatinous animals that are only distantly related to jellyfish.","indent":0}],"question":"Which statement, if true, would most directly weaken the claim by Caron and colleagues about the fossils found in China and the United States?","choices":["Sites in the Canadian Rockies from later periods than the Cambrian period have yielded fossils that have been conclusively identified as ctenophore fossils.","The fossils found in China and the United States are so poorly preserved that though they cannot be conclusively identified as jellyfish, they cannot be conclusively identified as ctenophores either.","While ctenophore fossils have been discovered in China and the United States, they have never been discovered in the Burgess Shale.","The fossils discovered by Caron and colleagues in the Burgess Shale were better preserved than the fossils discovered by other researchers in China and the United States."]},{"id":"b85c19ed","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"The violins handmade in the seventeenth century by Italian craftsman Antonio Stradivari have been celebrated as some of the finest in the world. In close collaboration with musicians, Stradivari introduced changes to the shape of a traditional violin, flattening some of the instrument’s curves and making ______ lighter overall.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The violins handmade in the seventeenth century by Italian craftsman Antonio Stradivari have been celebrated as some of the finest in the world.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"In close collaboration with musicians, Stradivari introduced changes to the shape of a traditional violin, flattening some of the instrument’s","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"curves and making ______ lighter overall.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["those","one","them","it"]},{"id":"60a4c088","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"What makes the theremin a unique musical instrument? You play it without touching it. When you place your ______ the pitch will shift as your hands move through the air.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["hand’s between the two antenna’s,","hands between the two antennas,","hands’ between the two antennas’,","hands’ between the two antennas,"]},{"id":"d198997b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Cy Twombly, a US painter and sculptor, created many large-scale abstract works, such as his 10-painting series Fifty Days at Iliam. In these works, Twombly’s artistic style is exemplified by his use of graffiti-like ______ often incorporate words or phrases from poetry and mythology.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Cy Twombly, a US painter and sculptor, created many large-scale abstract works, such as his 10-painting series Fifty Days at Iliam. In these works,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Twombly’s artistic style is exemplified by his use of graffiti-like ______ often incorporate words or phrases from poetry and mythology.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["scribbles: that","scribbles that","scribbles; that","scribbles. That"]},{"id":"9d4a701b","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Along with carbon dioxide concentration and temperature, light intensity affects the chemical reaction rate of ______ as light intensity increases, so does the rate at which the reactants (water and carbon dioxide) are converted into their products (glucose and oxygen).","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Along with carbon dioxide concentration and temperature, light intensity affects the chemical reaction rate of ______ as light intensity increases,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"so does the rate at which the reactants (water and carbon dioxide) are converted into their products (glucose and oxygen).","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["photosynthesis and","photosynthesis,","photosynthesis:","photosynthesis"]},{"id":"c06af4d8","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"Sociologist Alton Okinaka sits on the review board tasked with adding new sites to the Hawai‘i Register of Historic Places, which includes Ō Pi‘ilanihale Heiau and the ‘ paeka‘a Road Bridge. Okinaka doesn’t make such decisions ______ all historical designations must be approved by a group of nine other experts from the fields of architecture, archaeology, history, and Hawaiian culture.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Sociologist Alton Okinaka sits on the review board tasked with adding new sites to the Hawai‘i Register of Historic Places, which includes","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Pi‘ilanihale Heiau and the ‘Ōpaeka‘a Road Bridge. Okinaka doesn’t make such decisions ______ all historical designations must be approved by a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"group of nine other experts from the fields of architecture, archaeology, history, and Hawaiian culture.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["single-handedly, however;","single-handedly; however,","single-handedly, however,","single-handedly however"]},{"id":"486f03da","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Boundaries","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Boundaries","passage":"The short story “Rogue Enchantments” by Isabel Iba ez appears in Reclaim the ______ anthology of fantasy and science fiction written by authors of Latin American descent.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The short story “Rogue Enchantments” by Isabel Ibañez appears in Reclaim the______ anthology of fantasy and science fiction written by authors","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of Latin American descent.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["Stars. An","Stars, while an","Stars an","Stars, an"]},{"id":"a064955f","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In most deer species, males grow antlers, and females don’t. ______ reindeer are different. They are the only deer species in which the females grow antlers, too.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In most deer species, males grow antlers, and females don’t. ______ reindeer are different. They are the only deer species in which the females","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"grow antlers, too.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","Next,","However,","Thus,"]},{"id":"04ad68ca","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In Gothic architecture, flying buttresses are large arches that help support a building’s exterior walls. Before the Gothic era, cathedrals’ heavy ceilings had to be supported by thick, short walls, but the invention of flying buttresses eliminated this need. ______ Gothic cathedrals could be built with thinner, higher walls.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In Gothic architecture, flying buttresses are large arches that help support a building’s exterior walls. Before the Gothic era, cathedrals’ heavy","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ceilings had to be supported by thick, short walls, but the invention of flying buttresses eliminated this need. ______ Gothic cathedrals could be","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"built with thinner, higher walls.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","For instance,","Nevertheless,","As a result,"]},{"id":"f1631638","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Gaspar Enriquez is an artist. He specializes in portraits of Mexican Americans. A portrait is an artistic representation of a person. Enriquez completed a painting of the sculptor Luis Jimenez in 2003. He completed a drawing of the writer Rudolfo Anaya in 2016. The student wants to emphasize a difference between the two portraits.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Gaspar Enriquez is an artist.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"He specializes in portraits of Mexican Americans.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"A portrait is an artistic representation of a person.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Enriquez completed a painting of the sculptor Luis Jimenez in 2003.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"He completed a drawing of the writer Rudolfo Anaya in 2016.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The portraits, or artistic representations, of Luis Jimenez and Rudolfo Anaya were both completed by Enriquez in the early 2000s.","Enriquez has completed portraits of numerous Mexican Americans, including sculptor Luis Jimenez and writer Rudolfo Anaya.","While both are by Enriquez, the 2003 portrait of Luis Jimenez is a painting, and the 2016 portrait of Rudolfo Anaya is a drawing.","Luis Jimenez was a Mexican American sculptor, and Rudolfo Anaya was a Mexican American writer."]},{"id":"c4f7f726","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Many butterfly species have bold, brightly colored wings. ______ some butterfly species have wings that are almost completely colorless and transparent. Glasswing butterflies, for example, have see-through wings that make them nearly invisible.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Many butterfly species have bold, brightly colored wings. ______ some butterfly species have wings that are almost completely colorless and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"transparent. Glasswing butterflies, for example, have see-through wings that make them nearly invisible.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","Previously,","In other words,","However,"]},{"id":"ec03f090","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: A sestina is a thirty-nine-line poetic form. Each line of the poem ends with one of six end words, which alternate according to a set pattern. “Forage Sestina” is a sestina by Marilyn Hacker. Its end words are words, structure, wire, beam, wall, and room. “Towards Autumn” is a sestina by Marilyn Hacker. Its end words are daughter, friend, bread, mother, lover, and myself. The student wants to use one of the poems to illustrate the sestina form.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"A sestina is a thirty-nine-line poetic form.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Each line of the poem ends with one of six end words, which alternate according to a set pattern.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"“Forage Sestina” is a sestina by Marilyn Hacker.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Its end words are words, structure, wire, beam, wall, and room.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"“Towards Autumn” is a sestina by Marilyn Hacker.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Its end words are daughter, friend, bread, mother, lover, and myself.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Hacker employs the sestina, a poetic form with thirty-nine lines and six end words, in both “Forage Sestina” and “Towards Autumn.”","As a sestina, “Towards Autumn” contains thirty-nine lines and six end words — in this case, daughter, friend, bread, mother, lover, and myself— that alternate in a set pattern.","The thirty-nine-line sestina form uses the words daughter, friend, bread, mother, lover, and myself, which are found in the poem “Forage Sestina.”","Hacker has used the sestina form multiple times, as in “Towards Autumn,” which contains these six words: words, structure, wire, beam, wall, and room."]},{"id":"1c6e1d55","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Historically, most conductors of major orchestras and opera companies have been European men, but a new, more diverse generation of artists is stepping up to the podium. Mexico’s Alondra de la Parra took over as conductor for the Queensland Symphony Orchestra in 2017, ______ and Colombia’s Lina Gonzalez-Granados did the same for the Los Angeles Opera in 2022.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Historically, most conductors of major orchestras and opera companies have been European men, but a new, more diverse generation of artists","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"is stepping up to the podium. Mexico’s Alondra de la Parra took over as conductor for the Queensland Symphony Orchestra in 2017, ______ and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Colombia’s Lina Gonzalez-Granados did the same for the Los Angeles Opera in 2022.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["in addition,","lastly,","granted,","for instance,"]}];
